{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BLi7y77PA1uY5xBcznEePq","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# ProofDesk\n2\t\n3\t**Your work. Their feedback. One clear workflow.**\n4\t\n5\tProofDesk lets architecture practices present design work, collect structured client feedback, manage revision rounds and record approval of the exact submission reviewed.\n6\t\n7\tA supervised multi-agent system builds it: a supervisor agent plans and gates the work, parallel builder agents implement tickets, and separate reviewer and QA agents verify each PR. A human product owner approves anything going to production.\n8\t\n9\t## Repository map\n10\t\n11\t| Path | Contents |\n12\t|---|---|\n13\t| `product/` | Product documentation: scope, product knowledge, SRS, research, future considerations |\n14\t| `agent-system/` | **Reusable multi-agent delivery system** (supervisor, hooks, templates). Self-contained and project-neutral, so it can be extracted as its own product. See `agent-system/README.md` |\n15\t| `docs/delivery/` | ProofDesk's configuration of that system: project profile, operating defaults, decision log |\n16\t| `docs/adr/` | Architecture Decision Records |\n17\t| `docs/plans/` | Phase plans and gate checklists |\n18\t| `.claude/` | Claude Code wiring: agent symlinks into `agent-system/`, guard hook settings |\n19\t| `.github/` | PR template (CI workflows come with the boilerplate) |\n20\t\n21\t## Running the supervisor\n22\t\n23\t```bash\n24\tclaude --agent supervisor\n25\t```\n26\t\n27\t## Status\n28\t\n29\tPhase 0, Foundation: defining the SRS, stack, boilerplate and environment plan. Application code has not started.\n30\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01F4m15EqX5GFcD9DxfFoykh","session_id":"2a1bb233-54be-4a8f-827d-9e41acdf8ee6","timestamp":"2026-11-24T08:15:22.514Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Read README first heading"}
